title: Walk_Augustine_Socrates
tags: walk
speaker: Augustine
---
Augustine: We turn our steps back toward the central clearing.
Augustine: You have examined doubt, certainty, and the foundations of knowledge.
Augustine: Dappled light falls across the forest floor as we walk.
Augustine: True understanding requires aligning our inner mind with eternal wisdom.
Augustine: Even in virtual realms, the mind seeks truth beyond mere appearances.
Augustine: Socrates waits beneath his canopy to hear what you learned.
Augustine: Tell him whether doubt cleared your vision or deepened your questions.
Augustine: Every inquiry brings us closer to evaluating what really matters.
Augustine: Keep your mind focused on the highest truth as we return.
Augustine: Socrates will be ready to receive your final thoughts.
===
